  "generated_text": "To solve for \\( x \\) given the system of linear equations\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n3x + 4y - 12z &= 10, \\\\\n-2x - 3y + 9z &= -4,\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nwe will use the method of elimination. First, we will eliminate \\( y \\) by making the coefficients of \\( y \\) in both equations equal in magnitude but opposite in sign.\n\n1. **Multiply the first equation by 3 and the second equation by 4 to align the coefficients of \\( y \\):**\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n3(3x + 4y - 12z) &= 3(10), \\\\\n4(-2x - 3y + 9z) &= 4(-4).\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nThis gives us:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n9x + 12y - 36z &= 30, \\\\\n-8x - 12y + 36z &= -16.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n2. **Add the two equations to eliminate \\( y \\):**\n\n\\[\n(9x + 12y - 36z) + (-8x - 12y + 36z) = 30 + (-16).\n\\]\n\nSimplifying this, we get:\n\n\\[\n9x - 8x = 14 \\implies x = 14.\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( x \\) is \\(\\boxed{14}\\).",
